# AI agent routing policy

All agent orchestration decisions MUST go through `app/services/ai/policies/agent_routing.py` (`AgentRoutingPolicy`).

## Do

- Let the LLM choose tools from prompts + conversation history (`tool_choice="auto"`).
- Route execution via `AgentRoutingPolicy.decide_fast_path_plan()` — fast path only when the LLM returns `execution_mode="fast_path"` with high confidence; default is full ReAct.
- Use structural guards only: form-builder panel, UI source toggles, loop prevention (dedupe/pagination caps), explicit user source directives (`user_forbids_documents`).
- Add per-turn prompt supplements via `AgentRoutingPolicy.turn_system_prompt_supplement()` (page context, table requests, source toggles).

## Do not

- Auto-run fast path before the LLM routing decision (no keyword/heuristic hijacks).
- Add regex/keyword lists that force `search_documents`, `get_indicator_value`, or other tools based on query phrasing.
- Block `finish` or inject nudges to force tools on keyword match.
- Rewrite user queries with regex follow-up matchers in `query_rewriter.py`.

Loop guards stay in `tool_routing_policy.py` (dedupe, pagination). LLM guidance stays in `prompt_policy.py`.
